As a Lead Geophysics Engineer, evolving a basic acoustic generator into a production-ready Seismic Vibroseis Truck Array Controller requires a deterministic, highly synchronized control architecture. The fundamental objective is to coordinate four heavy-duty (60,000 lb) hydraulic vibrators to act as a single phased array. This maximizes P-wave penetration while eliminating destructive interference caused by phase misalignment between trucks.

Below is a robust, enterprise-grade IEC 61131-3 Structured Text (ST) implementation of the FB_VibroseisArrayController. It incorporates a linear frequency sweep (chirp) generator (10Hz to 100Hz), phase-locked loop (PLL) synchronization for 4 trucks, and hydraulic mass acceleration feedback control.

### IEC 61131-3 Structured Text Implementation

`pascal
TYPE
